### Lot 2 demo, organizer side: B4 live gates, close, B5 reconciliation and its CSV (IntelliJ HTTP client).
#
# Start the backend with the dev profile (dev seed: ATLAS FC, admin +212600000001):
#   docker compose up -d && SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev ./gradlew bootRun
# Gate calls (/gate/**) need an ECDSA P-256 device signature: run them from the scanner app, not from here.
# Sell tickets with lot1-sale.http, enrol and assign the scanners in the back-office (B6, B2), scan, then run these.
# OTP codes are printed by the dev log sender ([dev OTP] +2126... -> 123456): paste into @orgCode.

@base = http://localhost:8080/v1
@org = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@adminPhone = +212600000001
@orgCode = 000000
@eventId = 1

### 1. Organizer: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}"}

### 2. Organizer: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}", "code": "{{orgCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("orgToken", response.body.token); %}

### 3. B4: live gates (the back-office refetches this every 5 s)
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/live
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 4. B5 before the close: provisional (final = false, every assigned device unsynced)
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/reconciliation
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 5. Close (at or after starts_at). Devices drain, wipe and ack on their next sync.
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 6. B5: final once every assigned device has acked
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/reconciliation
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 7. B5: CSV export (; separated, UTF-8 with BOM)
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/reconciliation.csv
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
